From 45f00fb4f50ab99e15297a7f97d8fa97fae2c023 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 08:01:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tools/dvbridge: drawn_over() decodes the picture under a
 pixel once

The conversion of a pixel drawn over back to the codes of the source transport took the picture
under it from picture_at(), and the test of which form of the conversion is exact decoded the same
codes again. Compilers need not merge the two: through D3D12, the integrated Radeon of a Ryzen 9
7950X3D made both, four PQ round trips for a pixel of a profile 5 picture where three do. The
picture under the pixel is now the clamped value of that one decode(), which is what picture_at()
returns for it.

Measured with a host test of the bridge (frames of three profile 5 pictures, two profile 7 FEL
pictures and one profile 8.1 picture with Kodi's GUI composited over them by Kodi's own composite,
162 frames: nine GUI drawings at two GUI sizes, and three of them with what is drawn over not
known, with the picture made whole first, and packed the right way up): the same bytes as before
on lavapipe and on both GPUs of the PC, the integrated Radeon and an RTX 4080 SUPER, through
D3D12. On the integrated Radeon a profile 5 frame under the player information took 83.1 ms and
takes 76.7 ms (a window over a dimmed screen, 101.9 and 93.0 ms); profile 7 FEL and 8.1 under the
player information, 35.4 and 30.2 ms before, 33.7 and 28.5 ms now. Radeonsi, the driver of that
GPU in LibreELEC, is not verified.
---
 tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_source.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_source.c b/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_source.c
index 8d7239b..9415a0b 100644
--- a/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_source.c
+++ b/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_source.c
@@ -427,13 +427,17 @@ static const char PACK[] =
     "vec3 drawn_over(ivec2 p, vec4 d)\n"
     "{\n"
     "    float a = 2.0 - d.a;\n"
-    "    vec3 codes = codes_at(p), under = picture_at(p);\n"
+    /* (Hades: the picture under the pixel, as picture_at() has it, from the decode() that the test
+     * below takes, not from a second one: compilers need not merge the two, and the D3D12 one of an
+     * integrated Radeon made both, a tenth of the packing's time under a GUI over the whole raster) */
+    "    vec3 codes = codes_at(p);\n"
+    "    vec3 raw = inside(p.x, p.y) ? decode(codes) : vec3(0.0);\n"
+    "    vec3 under = clamp(raw, 0.0, 1.0);\n"
     /* the first form where decoding is invertible: affine, whatever the picture clamps; else with
      * T' within [0, 1] and the picture not clamped */
     "    bool exact = affine != 0;\n"
     "    if (!exact) {\n"
     "        vec3 tp = ycc_forward * (codes / code_scale - ycc_offset);\n"
-    "        vec3 raw = inside(p.x, p.y) ? decode(codes) : vec3(0.0);\n"
     "        exact = all(greaterThanEqual(tp, vec3(0.0))) && all(lessThanEqual(tp, vec3(1.0))) &&\n"
     "                raw == under;\n"
     "    }\n"
-- 
